        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-29T06:18:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no APF filtering on tethered interfaces, so the multicast lock does not control APF multicast filtering on these. This code tries to make sure that APF doesn\u0027t filter out packets, so I think taking the lock isn\u0027t needed on downstream tethering (it would increase power consumption on other interfaces without really helping with the downstream interface).\n\nAdded a comment.",
      "parentUuid": "c4e295d2_5ae53a89",
